# Refresh the panel's media cache after a RESUME from suspend (OI-16, the Owner
# chose option (a) 2026-07-29): with SLEEP_MODE=suspend the panel suspends every
# night and resumes every morning WITHOUT booting, so a boot-only sync goes stale
# for weeks. This hook makes every resume behave like a boot for freshness.
#
# HOW THE HOOK WORKS — the standard systemd resume pattern:
#   WantedBy=suspend.target pulls this unit into the suspend transaction;
#   After=suspend.target orders it after that target is REACHED — and
#   suspend.target is only reached when systemd-suspend.service completes, i.e.
#   when the machine has already WOKEN. So this unit starts at resume, never at
#   suspend time. Type=oneshot with no RemainAfterExit means it falls back to
#   inactive immediately, so every later suspend/resume cycle fires it again.
#
# WHY `--no-block` IS LOAD-BEARING, not a flourish: this unit runs INSIDE the
# resume transaction. A plain `systemctl start` waits for the started job to
# finish, and a first full mirror over 802.11 is allowed up to an hour
# (TimeoutStartSec in wall-sync.service) — that wait would hold the resume
# transaction open for the whole sync. `--no-block` only ENQUEUES the job and
# returns at once: this hook is done in milliseconds, the wake is never delayed,
# and wall-sync.service then runs detached as its own job with its own journal,
# its own timeout and its own pass/fail status (`journalctl -u wall-sync`).
#
# THE Wi-Fi RACE, honestly: network-online.target was reached at BOOT and stays
# active across suspend, so no ordering here can wait for the radio to
# re-associate — that takes a few seconds after wake. wall-sync.sh therefore does
# its own short bounded wait (nm-online, 30 s cap) before mounting; if the network
# is still not up after that, the mount fails LOUDLY (failed unit + journal) and
# the retry is the documented on-demand command: sudo systemctl start wall-sync.
#
# Only suspend.target: the panel's one sleep path is `systemctl suspend` from
# wall-sleep.sh (SLEEP_MODE=suspend). It never hibernates — no hibernate/
# hybrid-sleep targets are listed because no code path can reach them.
[Unit]
Description=Wall panel: refresh the media cache after resume (OI-16a)
Documentation=file:///opt/wall-panel/stack/autoinstall/wall/README.md
After=suspend.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/systemctl start --no-block wall-sync.service
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal

[Install]
WantedBy=suspend.target
